---
import { version } from "../../../../npm/magistr/package.json";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Workflow from "../components/Workflow.astro";
import ProductEvidence from "../components/ProductEvidence.astro";
import ProjectTour from "../components/ProjectTour.astro";
const description = "Build bigger projects with your coding agent. Magistr keeps the roadmap, recorded reasoning, work chunks and checks together so you can keep going.";
const jsonLd = [
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebSite","name":"Magistr","url":"https://magistr.dev",description},
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Magistr","applicationCategory":"DeveloperApplication","operatingSystem":"macOS (Apple Silicon)","softwareVersion":version,description,"url":"https://magistr.dev","downloadUrl":"https://magistr.dev/docs/installation","softwareRequirements":"macOS 15 or later, Rust 1.95 or later, repository access"}
];
---
<Base title="Build a project with Magistr" description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero section-shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-main">
        <h1 id="hero-title">Build a project with Magistr.</h1>
        <p class="hero-subtitle">Work with the coding agent you prefer.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="builder-note" aria-labelledby="builder-title">
        <h2 id="builder-title" class="sr-only">Why I’m building this</h2>
        <p>I’m building Magistr to work on bigger projects without starting over in every chat.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="#product">Explore how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          <a id="install-btn" class="text-link" href="#install">Install Magistr</a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section id="product" class="section-shell section-block product-section" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="product-title">
      <h2 id="product-title" class="sr-only">Keep the whole project in view.</h2>
      <ProjectTour />
    </section>

    <section id="workflow" class="section-shell section-block example-section" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-eyebrow">A complete recorded build</p>
        <h2 id="workflow-title">Here’s what working through a project looks like.</h2>
        <p>A support inbox with threaded mail, search, assignment, and the cases that make it interesting: repeated deliveries and two people changing the same request. Follow the actual work, including the failed checks and the fixes.</p>
      </div>
      <Workflow />
    </section>

    <section id="keep-going" class="section-shell section-block continuation" aria-labelledby="continue-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="continue-title">You get to keep building.</h2>
        <p>The first working version gives you something to try. Use it, spot what’s missing, and decide what you want to do next.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="continuation-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>Give the next idea somewhere to go.</h3>
          <p>Save feedback while you’re in the middle of something else. Investigate it, connect it to what you’ve learned, and put the useful changes on the roadmap.</p>
          <ol class="feedback-path" aria-label="From feedback to planned work"><li>Something feels wrong</li><li>Find out why</li><li>Update the plan</li></ol>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/roadmap#make-room-for-feedback">Work with feedback ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Come back with the next session.</h3>
          <p>Your project keeps its roadmap, saved decisions, progress and check results. A fresh agent can read them, look at the current code, and pick up the unfinished work.</p>
          <div class="session-handoff"><span>Session ends</span><strong>Plan · Decisions · Work · Checks</strong><span>Next session reads the project</span></div>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/concepts#pick-up-in-another-session">See what carries over ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Work in the real code.</h3>
          <p>Magistr gives your agent tools to find and read source, check that a file hasn’t changed underneath an edit, and keep a journal of its changes.</p>
          <div class="source-sequence" aria-label="Source workflow"><code>Read the file</code><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><code>Check the edit</code><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><code>Save the change</code></div>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/concepts#work-in-your-source">Source changes and undo ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Choose how far the agent goes.</h3>
          <p>Finish one chunk, or give a longer run a focus and a limit. A fresh session for each chunk keeps the next piece grounded in the saved plan.</p>
          <pre class="loop-command"><code>magistr next-loop --agent codex --max-iterations 5</code></pre>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/chunks#work-through-a-longer-run">Run a few chunks ↗</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="agents" class="section-shell section-block agent-section" aria-labelledby="agents-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="agents-title">Bring the agent you like working with.</h2>
        <p>Codex and Claude Code have project setup and workflows ready to use. Other agents can connect through MCP. Your model account and permissions stay with your agent.</p>
        <a class="text-link section-link" href="/docs/installation#connect-another-agent">Connect your agent ↗</a>
      </div>
      <details id="evidence" class="example-sessions recorded-example">
        <summary>See real Codex, Claude Code and desktop sessions</summary>
        <p>These October 19 captures follow a separate, small Python fix. Each one says what that session actually did.</p>
        <ProductEvidence />
      </details>
    </section>

    <section id="install" class="section-shell section-block install-section" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="install-title">
      <div class="install-grid">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="install-title">Install the source preview</h2>
          <p>v{version} is available to people with <a href="https://github.com/AlrikOlson/magistr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">repository access<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>. Registry packages are not published yet.</p>
          <p>You'll need Apple Silicon macOS 15 or later, Rust 1.95 or later, Git, and the macOS command-line build tools. Bring your own Codex or Claude Code account.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/installation">Full installation instructions</a>
        </div>
        <div class="code-panel">
          <div class="code-label"><span>In your terminal</span><button class="copy-button" type="button" aria-label="Copy commands" data-copy="source-install" hidden>Copy commands</button></div>
          <pre id="source-install"><code>git clone https://github.com/AlrikOlson/magistr.git
cd magistr
cargo install --locked --path crates/magistr-cli
magistr --version</code></pre>
          <p class="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="install-next">Run <code>magistr init .</code> in the project you want to build. Setup connects your agent and helps you choose the project’s checks. Setup does not start implementation. Open a session, talk through the project, and use <code>magistr next</code> when you’re ready for the first chunk.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
<script is:inline>
  document.querySelectorAll("[data-copy]").forEach((button) => {
    button.hidden = false;
    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const source = document.getElementById(button.dataset.copy);
      const status = button.closest(".code-panel")?.querySelector(".copy-status");
      if (!source || !status) return;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(source.textContent);
        status.textContent = "Commands copied.";
      } catch {
        status.textContent = "Copy is unavailable. Select the commands above to copy them.";
      }
    });
  });
</script>
